UID:7647eb052ff89638@role-civil-litigation-appellate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20261123T172559Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261109
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Mullin v. Friends of the Ruidosa Church
DESCRIPTION:_________________ \n_________________ \n1  Cite as: 610 U. S. 
 ____ (2026) \nPer Curiam \nSUPREME COURT OF THE UNITED STATES \nNo. 26A560
  \nMARKWAYNE MULLIN\, SECRETARY OF HOMELAND \nSECURITY\, ET AL. v. FRIENDS
  OF THE \nRUIDOSA CHURCH\, ET AL. \nON APPLICATION FOR STAY \n[November 9\
 , 2026]\n PER CURIAM. \nSection 102 of the Illegal Immigration Reform and 
 Immi-\ngrant Responsibility Act of 1996 (IIRIRA) grants the Secre-\ntary o
 f Homeland Security broad authority to construct bor-\nder barriers and ro
 ads “to deter illegal crossings in areas of \nhigh illegal entry into th
 e United States.”  §102(a)\, 110 Stat.\n3009–554\, as amended\, note 
 following 8 U. S. C. §1103.  The \nsame section expressly authorizes the 
 Secretary “ ‘to waive\nall legal requirements’ ” as “ ‘necessa
 ry to ensure expedi-\ntious construction’ ” of those barriers and road
 s\, §102(c)(1)\,\n119 Stat. 306\, and sharply limits judicial review of a
 ll \nclaims arising from such waiver determinations.  Specifi -\ncally\, t
 he statute provides that “‘[a] cause of action or claim \nmay only be 
 brought alleging a violation of the Constitution\nof the United States’ 
 ” and courts “ ‘shall not have jurisdic-\ntion’” over nonconstit
 utional claims.  §102(c)(2)(A).\nEarlier this year\, the Secretary invoke
 d Section 102’s\nwaiver authority to initiate a border-construction proj
 ect at \nthe U. S.–Mexico border\, in a region that U. S. Customs and \n
 Border Protection has designated the “Big Bend Sector.”\nThe Secretary
  found that the Big Bend Sector “is an area of\nhigh illegal entry” re
 quiring additional border barriers\, and \nwaived the application of a var
 iety of environmental and \nconservation laws to facilitate expeditious co
 nstruction. \n \n  \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \
 n \n \n2 MULLIN v. FRIENDS OF THE RUIDOSA CHURCH \nPer Curiam \nSee 91 Fed
 . Reg. 7298 (2026)\, as amended by id.\, at 40550\; \nid.\, at 27969\, as 
 amended by id.\, at 34831\; id.\, at 46939. \nShortly thereafter\, respond
 ents—an individual river \nguide\, an environmental nonprofit\, and a no
 nprofit o\nhttps://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/26pdf/26a560_onkq.pdf
URL:https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/26pdf/26a560_onkq.pdf
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
